workspace matches 96afc2c75 in many respects (it has lifecycleStatus on most specs). Let me confirm whether the workspace equals 96afc2c75 tree except for my changes. Actually the workspace's O02 spec lacks lifecycleStatus while 96afc2c75... let me check.\n\nLet me verify whether base==874befaaa content matches workspace. Let's check a file.\n\nActually the important thing is just to report accurately.\n\nLet me quickly compare: does the workspace O02 spec match base's? Both lack lifecycleStatus. And does 96afc2c75 have it? Let me check.\n\nLet me also confirm the harness spec-lifecycle test passes on the pristine workspace (before my change) — i.e., it's really pre-existing. Let me check base trial's agent dir: does it have the o02 spec and does it lack lifecycleStatus? Yes, base agent dir has harness/specs/tasks/lifecycle...? Let me just check base agent spec dir.\n\nActually simplest: the failing file is harness-gap-trace-cost-sampling.md which I did not touch. Confirmed pre-existing by checking base copy lacks lifecycleStatus. Good.\n\nLet me quickly verify the workspace state of that file equals base."}}
