{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_288","type":"agent_message","text":"Implementation complete. Here is the structured result.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"summary\": \"Implemented E01 reliability aggregation in the Agent Dev benefit report. Added a side-effect-free aggregator (scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs + .d.mts), a pre-registered deterministic fixture (shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json: k=3, minCases=20, flakeThreshold=0.01, 5 cases), wired it into scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs (reads the fixture, emits a `reliability` block in report.json/report.md), and added the task spec, boundary rule, unit test, closure doc, acceptance record and digest manifest under the packet's targetScope. The aggregator keeps pass^k (all-k pass fraction of complete cases) and pass@k (at-least-one) separate; missing/timeout/crash/skip make a case `incomplete`, are preserved and excluded from denominators; flake = first-scheduled-trial failure with a later re-run success (first failure preserved; safety-required cases must be 0 skip/0 flake); positive anchors must all-pass and negative anchors all-reject or gate=fail; below minCases the gate is `insufficient-sample` rather than PASS. Fixture is labelled a deterministic oracle (no live provider / human / generalization claim). Product defaults, locks and approval semantics were not touched; no scheduled automation added. Observed fixture result: complete 4/5, incomplete 1, perTrial 0.5, pass^k 0.25, pass@k 0.75, flake 0.25, gate insufficient-sample. README (en/zh/ja/ru) reviewed: only an internal evaluation report changed, so no user-visible interface/config text requires an update (recorded in e01-acceptance.json). Note: this trial workspace ships without .git, so no commit/tree identity is claimed and the harness diff-based gate cannot resolve origin/main; a junction to a reusable installed node_modules was used to run the dependency-light gates (no dependency install, no network) and removed afterward.\",\n  \"testsRun\": [\n    \"node scripts/check-no-bom.mjs -> ok\",\n    \"node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 -> 1 file passed, 6 passed / 6\",\n    \"node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run tests/unit/harness-specs.test.ts tests/unit/harness-spec-portability.test.ts tests/unit/docs-index.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 -> 3 files passed, 52 passed / 52\",\n    \"node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run tests/unit/harness-spec-lifecycle.test.ts -> 1 pre-existing failure: 'harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-trace-cost-sampling.md: missing required field lifecycleStatus' (base O02 spec, unchanged by this packet and byte-identical to base; not caused by my change)\",\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md --no-diff -> 'Spec is valid'\",\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs context --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md -> exit 0, no missing scenarios/rules\",\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs run --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md --dry-run -> environment-blocked: 'invalid or missing diff base ref: origin/main' (workspace has no git metadata; not a spec defect)\",\n    \"node node_modules/eslint/bin/eslint.js scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.d.mts tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts -> exit 0 (1 warning: 'file ignored' for the .d.mts, no matching config)\",\n    \"node node_modules/@typescript/native-preview/bin/tsgo.js --noEmit -p tsconfig.test.json --composite false -> exit 2 (900 lines) with 900 pre-existing errors; also reproduced identically on the pristine base tree, and a search for reliability-aggregation/agent-dev-benefit-eval/e01/reliability-fixture in the output found 0 matches (no new errors introduced)\",\n    \"node scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs -> exit 0; report.json carries report.reliability = {k:3, completeCaseCount:4, incompleteCaseCount:1, passK:0.25, passAtK:0.75, perTrialSuccessRate:0.5, flakeRate:0.25, gate:'insufficient-sample'}\",\n    \"node -e aggregateReliability assertions over the fixture (passK/passAtK split, incomplete preservation, flake semantics, insufficient-sample) -> ALL NODE-LEVEL ASSERTIONS PASSED\",\n    \"node scripts/verify-evidence digest round-trip over docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/E01-SHA256SUMS -> 8 entries, 0 mismatches (SHA256SUMS re-readable)\",\n    \"credential scan (regex: sk-/AKIA/PRIVATE KEY/ghp_/xox/phc_) over the 9 changed files -> files=9 hits=0\",\n    \"node -e JSON.parse over docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-acceptance.json -> parses OK\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nFiles written (packet targetScope): `scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs`, `scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs`, `scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.d.mts`, `shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json`, `tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts`, `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md`, `harness/specs/rules/reliability-aggregation-boundary.md`, `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-reliability-aggregation.md`, `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-acceptance.json`, `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/E01-SHA256SUMS`.\n\nTwo honesty notes recorded in the acceptance record rather than claimed as done: (1) registering the three retained E01 doc files in `scripts/repository-artifacts.json`/`.gitignore` is outside this packet's `targetScope` and impossible to verify here (`repo:artifacts:check` needs `.git`), so it is listed as a follow-up; (2) generated `artifacts/agent-dev-benefit-eval/report.json` is local-only output and was not tracked (and was cleaned up)."}}
